.TH CTI-FALCON 1 "2026-11-18" "cti-agent" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-falcon \- check the fleet's CrowdStrike Falcon API client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti\-falcon \-\-check
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR DURATION ]
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-falcon \-\-check
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cti-falcon
is a read-only check, run by hand. It is the first step of advisory triage
from the organisation's own data. Triage will read three things from Falcon:
the applications we run, which hosts saw an indicator, and which ATT&CK
techniques our detections fired on. Before any of that is built,
.B \-\-check
proves the API client works.
.PP
It gets an OAuth2 token, then makes one
.B limit=1
read per scope on the exact route triage will call:
.TP
.B Hosts: READ
.I /devices/queries/devices/v1
.TP
.B Assets: READ
.I /discover/queries/applications/v1
(Falcon Discover). A 403 here when the scope is ticked means Discover is not
licensed.
.TP
.B IOC Management: READ
.I /iocs/queries/indicators/devices/v1
for the reserved domain
.BR example.com .
The service's own 404 (its JSON answer, with a trace ID) is the expected
"no hosts" answer and counts as OK. A 404 for the route itself, or one from
anything in front of the service, is an ERROR.
.TP
.B Alerts: READ
.I /alerts/queries/alerts/v2
.PP
For each it prints OK, DENIED or ERROR, with a count at most. It then revokes
its token. It never prints the token, the secret, an ID or a record.
.SH OPTIONS
Go's flag syntax: each option may also be written with a single dash.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Required. Run the check.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the result as JSON instead of text.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DURATION"
Give up after this long. Default: 2m.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Read from the environment, or from
.I fleet.env
.RB ( FLEET_ENV ,
or
.I fleet.env
under
.BR FLEET_HOME ).
There is no flag for the secret.
.TP
.B FALCON_BASE_URL
The cloud's API host:
.BR api.crowdstrike.com ,
.BR api.us\-2.crowdstrike.com ,
.B api.eu\-1.crowdstrike.com
or
.BR api.laggar.gcw.crowdstrike.com .
Any other host, a port, a path or credentials in the URL is refused before
a request is made. Redirects are never followed.
.TP
.B FALCON_CLIENT_ID
.TQ
.B FALCON_CLIENT_SECRET
The API client, created with Read scopes only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The token and all four scopes work.
.TP
.B 1
A setting is missing or refused, the token failed, or a scope is denied or
failed.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage, including running without
.BR \-\-check .
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the client on the box:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-falcon \-\-check
.RE
.PP
The same, as JSON, for a script:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo cti\-agent cti\-falcon \-\-check \-\-json
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cti\-agent (1),
RUNBOOK.md section 11j, SECURITY.md.
